WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.327 --> 00:00:08.208
In 2015,

00:00:08.689 --> 00:00:10.912
A mysterious virus is striking South America.

00:00:11.692 --> 00:00:13.655
He was talking about Zika.

00:00:14.175 --> 00:00:15.115
the Zika virus.

00:00:16.517 --> 00:00:19.221
Hundreds of babies are born with severe mental disabilities.

00:00:20.161 --> 00:00:22.083
Once we understood what this virus was capable of,

00:00:22.285 --> 00:00:23.445
We became genuinely worried.

00:00:24.827 --> 00:00:27.149
This is the untold story of a world war.

00:00:27.951 --> 00:00:32.055
There was an army of scientists to fight this virus.

00:00:33.617 --> 00:00:35.119
This is how science helped me.

00:00:35.119 --> 00:00:36.360
leading the fight against the virus.

00:00:38.062 --> 00:00:39.823
And the creature that transmits it.

00:00:40.784 --> 00:00:42.265
We remove the tube and inside,

00:00:42.385 --> 00:00:43.667
There's this tiny little brain.

00:00:43.768 --> 00:00:46.929
We didn't really understand what was happening because it was completely unexpected.

00:00:48.111 --> 00:00:50.292
Zika is the new enemy to defeat.

00:00:52.015 --> 00:00:52.955
The more we learned,

00:00:53.176 --> 00:00:53.876
The more we told each other,

00:00:54.236 --> 00:00:54.777
Oh my god,

00:00:54.816 --> 00:00:55.757
That's still a surprise.

00:01:14.502 --> 00:01:15.403
Early 2015,

00:01:15.923 --> 00:01:21.727
Dr. Patricia Brasil sees many women arriving at her clinic in Rio de Janeiro with strange symptoms.

00:01:27.533 --> 00:01:28.414
She wasn't doing badly.

00:01:29.495 --> 00:01:32.938
She didn't have that appearance that one usually has when one is severely ill.

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:39.245
It was a disease that just gave you a rash and very strong itching.

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:48.254
Dr. Brazil's patients all live in the favelas of Rio.

00:01:53.159 --> 00:01:53.960
Irlana Cabral,

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:55.140
aged 19,

00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:56.221
is one of them.

00:01:58.662 --> 00:02:01.564
Irlana had a slight, barely visible rash.

00:02:02.865 --> 00:02:04.686
A redness that disappears in a few days.

00:02:07.709 --> 00:02:11.230
We didn't know exactly what it was and we were trying to establish a diagnosis.

00:02:13.051 --> 00:02:13.611
But little by little,

00:02:14.292 --> 00:02:17.093
Hundreds of thousands of new cases are being reported across Brazil.

00:02:18.134 --> 00:02:19.435
The doctors are distraught.

00:02:21.216 --> 00:02:22.817
By analyzing the blood of these women,

00:02:23.297 --> 00:02:25.439
They detect an unknown virus in South America.

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:27.100
They stumble upon

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:27.881
Zika.

00:02:30.462 --> 00:02:31.443
I found a report.

00:02:31.723 --> 00:02:33.865
I compared it to what my patients presented.

00:02:33.905 --> 00:02:34.565
And I thought to myself,

00:02:34.905 --> 00:02:36.346
It's exactly the same thing.

00:02:36.667 --> 00:02:37.607
It must be Zika.

00:02:41.029 --> 00:02:43.951
Brazilian doctors are not the only ones concerned about Zika.

00:02:54.425 --> 00:02:56.506
The first time I heard about Zika,

00:02:57.706 --> 00:02:59.788
That was when the new epidemic broke out in Brazil.

00:03:00.929 --> 00:03:05.931
That interested me a lot and I wanted to know more about what Zika was like before he reached Brazil.

00:03:07.853 --> 00:03:11.275
Anthony Fauci is one of the top medical researchers in the United States.

00:03:15.198 --> 00:03:18.360
Even he had to go back into the archives to learn more about Zika.

00:03:20.827 --> 00:03:23.769
Zika was first identified in 1947.

00:03:24.409 --> 00:03:27.670
but no cases of the disease in humans were observed before 1952.

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:28.831
Afterwards,

00:03:28.991 --> 00:03:30.072
in Africa and Asia,

00:03:30.631 --> 00:03:31.592
It has more or less disappeared.

00:03:35.073 --> 00:03:36.754
The virus was discovered here.

00:03:37.094 --> 00:03:37.614
in Uganda,

00:03:38.235 --> 00:03:39.915
in the heart of a forest called Zika.

00:03:44.077 --> 00:03:44.798
In 60 years,

00:03:45.378 --> 00:03:47.819
Only 14 infections have been reported worldwide.

00:03:50.695 --> 00:03:51.657
None of them were serious.

00:03:52.418 --> 00:03:52.618
Then,

00:03:52.859 --> 00:03:53.580
in 2007,

00:03:54.181 --> 00:03:56.023
Zika appeared in the Pacific.

00:03:56.264 --> 00:03:57.025
on Yap Island.

00:03:59.187 --> 00:04:00.169
And in 2013,

00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:02.031
in French Polynesia.

00:04:04.137 --> 00:04:06.299
We were receiving reports of cases in French Polynesia.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:09.300
That was before the disease arrived in Brazil.

00:04:10.763 --> 00:04:11.502
But in Polynesia,

00:04:11.843 --> 00:04:12.544
80%

00:04:12.544 --> 00:04:15.026
People who were infected had few or no symptoms.

00:04:17.249 --> 00:04:22.473
Everything we learned about Zika suggested that it was an infection without consequences.

00:04:36.812 --> 00:04:37.332
In France,

00:04:37.912 --> 00:04:43.634
Experts are looking into the Polynesian epidemic and discovering that Zika may not be completely harmless.

00:04:45.615 --> 00:04:46.515
During this epidemic,

00:04:46.916 --> 00:04:52.257
This was new and had not been seen in Micronesia on the island of Yap a few years earlier.

00:04:52.838 --> 00:04:59.980
This involved the onset of severe paralysis in approximately 40-50 patients who had to be hospitalized.

00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:02.461
because his paralysis was so severe that he could no longer breathe.

00:05:02.721 --> 00:05:04.221
This is what is known as Guillain-Barré syndrome.

00:05:05.942 --> 00:05:11.242
Guillain-Barré syndrome is a rare and poorly understood disease that causes a severe attack on the nervous system.

00:05:13.204 --> 00:05:17.004
Doctors are surprised by Zika's ability to trigger this syndrome.

00:05:19.045 --> 00:05:20.406
But among the infected adults,

00:05:20.906 --> 00:05:23.387
Less than one person in a thousand is affected by the disease.

00:05:25.047 --> 00:05:26.668
Zika therefore remains an enigma.

00:05:27.567 --> 00:05:32.331
We weren't too worried either because we were talking about a few dozen cases.

00:05:32.913 --> 00:05:33.733
We became interested in it,

00:05:34.314 --> 00:05:36.935
but without being particularly alarmist.

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:45.884
The cases of Guylain Barret in French Polynesia are not reassuring.

00:05:46.624 --> 00:05:47.564
But in 2015,

00:05:48.045 --> 00:05:50.966
No one yet suspects how dangerous Zika is.

00:05:52.887 --> 00:05:55.127
Thousands of babies have been born with brain damage.

00:05:55.367 --> 00:05:57.108
Brazil declares a state of emergency.

00:05:59.089 --> 00:06:01.110
Laura has microcephaly.

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:04.632
In the fall of 2015,

00:06:04.911 --> 00:06:05.853
a few months later,

00:06:06.452 --> 00:06:10.134
Hundreds of babies with malformed skulls are being born in Brazil.

00:06:11.855 --> 00:06:13.536
They suffer from microcephaly.

00:06:15.787 --> 00:06:19.668
A brain development defect that occurs in the early months of pregnancy.

00:06:21.168 --> 00:06:23.229
Around the sixth,

00:06:23.429 --> 00:06:25.030
tenth week of pregnancy,

00:06:25.390 --> 00:06:29.271
The cells that will give rise to the brain begin to multiply.

00:06:29.771 --> 00:06:32.532
So if an infection occurs during the first trimester,

00:06:32.752 --> 00:06:33.792
in these critical weeks,

00:06:34.312 --> 00:06:38.453
The risks that the brain may not develop normally are considerable.

00:06:38.613 --> 00:06:41.754
When a baby's head is of normal size,

00:06:42.434 --> 00:06:44.955
This is because the developing brain pushes against the skull.

00:06:45.555 --> 00:06:46.956
which forms the outline of the skull.

00:06:48.237 --> 00:06:50.278
If something disrupts this process,

00:06:51.399 --> 00:06:55.282
Then the brain does not develop properly and the skull remains small.

00:06:58.004 --> 00:07:03.687
This increase in the number of microcephalic babies is occurring at a time when Zika cases are multiplying.

00:07:07.050 --> 00:07:08.831
But is it really the virus that causes the disease?

00:07:11.593 --> 00:07:11.933
In Rio,

00:07:12.574 --> 00:07:14.655
Panic is spreading among pregnant women.

00:07:16.247 --> 00:07:18.729
Including the one followed by Dr. Patricia Brazil.

00:07:21.052 --> 00:07:22.012
I was very worried.

00:07:23.074 --> 00:07:25.576
The mothers who came for consultations were frightened.

00:07:26.296 --> 00:07:27.778
They were haunted by a ghost.

00:07:28.639 --> 00:07:30.260
The ghost of microcephaly.

00:07:32.302 --> 00:07:33.683
Will my baby be normal?

00:07:34.224 --> 00:07:34.865
What will it be like?

00:07:37.887 --> 00:07:40.971
Dr. Brazil then performed ultrasounds on all of these patients.

00:07:45.344 --> 00:07:47.065
The results are alarming.

00:07:48.685 --> 00:07:50.806
29%

00:07:50.986 --> 00:07:53.207
The babies of the women presented with malformations.

00:07:54.388 --> 00:07:55.308
I was devastated.

00:07:56.269 --> 00:07:59.550
I was truly desperate because I put myself in their shoes.

00:08:04.972 --> 00:08:05.292
In my opinion,

00:08:05.352 --> 00:08:06.113
as a mother,

00:08:06.213 --> 00:08:06.773
It's very difficult.

00:08:06.793 --> 00:08:08.134
And for them...

00:08:12.235 --> 00:08:12.515
Davy,

00:08:12.896 --> 00:08:13.776
Irlana's baby...

00:08:14.075 --> 00:08:15.876
was born with severe microcephaly.

00:08:19.018 --> 00:08:19.698
When my son was born,

00:08:20.579 --> 00:08:22.700
It was initially an extraordinary feeling.

00:08:25.382 --> 00:08:33.146
That feeling disappeared when I saw all those doctors arrive and take him away.

00:08:37.669 --> 00:08:40.690
The doctors tell him that Davy will never develop normally.

00:08:43.793 --> 00:08:47.776
I cried so much and I felt so guilty about it.

00:08:48.456 --> 00:08:49.637
But maternal feeling,

00:08:50.537 --> 00:08:51.358
It's inexplicable.

00:08:53.439 --> 00:08:55.399
It's a love that completely engulfs you.

00:09:00.364 --> 00:09:01.324
Across Brazil,

00:09:01.624 --> 00:09:03.566
Thousands of women are experiencing the same tragedy.

00:09:04.346 --> 00:09:06.888
And the cause of microcephaly is still not confirmed.

00:09:09.696 --> 00:09:12.397
Blood tests do not always reveal the presence of Zika.

00:09:13.537 --> 00:09:14.778
Yet he is the perfect scapegoat.

00:09:20.359 --> 00:09:23.679
The problem has reached proportions that are alarming experts worldwide.

00:09:27.561 --> 00:09:31.822
The discovery of neurological complications in children took us all by surprise.

00:09:32.482 --> 00:09:33.962
And we became genuinely worried.

00:09:35.644 --> 00:09:36.484
I remember it very well.

00:09:37.203 --> 00:09:38.724
I called an emergency meeting.

00:09:39.346 --> 00:09:39.665
I said,

00:09:40.386 --> 00:09:40.886
Okay guys,

00:09:41.126 --> 00:09:41.927
All hands on deck.

00:09:43.168 --> 00:09:44.208
We don't have much time,

00:09:44.889 --> 00:09:45.989
Women are infected,

00:09:46.510 --> 00:09:47.290
They become pregnant.

00:09:48.011 --> 00:09:49.132
Their children are in danger.

00:09:49.852 --> 00:09:51.153
We really need to act quickly.

00:09:56.877 --> 00:09:58.138
Early 2016,

00:09:58.139 --> 00:10:00.000
Scientists around the world are committed to...

00:10:00.059 --> 00:10:01.260
Fighting against this epidemic.

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:05.182
They come from different countries and different disciplines.

00:10:06.063 --> 00:10:08.384
They must answer three essential questions.

00:10:11.187 --> 00:10:14.248
Is Zika really the cause of microcephaly?

00:10:16.330 --> 00:10:21.173
How did this initially harmless virus transform into such a formidable enemy?

00:10:22.692 --> 00:10:23.153
And finally,

00:10:24.173 --> 00:10:25.355
How can we stop this scourge?

00:10:35.403 --> 00:10:36.745
Among all these questions,

00:10:37.404 --> 00:10:38.325
One thing is certain,

00:10:39.346 --> 00:10:42.408
The Zika virus is transmitted by mosquitoes.

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:48.552
When you put a mosquito under a microscope,

00:10:48.553 --> 00:10:50.995
We realize that it's a whole world that we have before our eyes.

00:10:51.474 --> 00:10:59.000
And we are going deeper and deeper into the functioning of the mosquito to better understand the role of mosquitoes in the transmission of pathogens.

00:11:03.156 --> 00:11:05.238
In a secure laboratory in Montpellier,

00:11:05.678 --> 00:11:08.520
Frédéric Simard breeds mosquitoes that carry Zika.

00:11:13.765 --> 00:11:16.227
This is the species Aedes aegypti,

00:11:17.027 --> 00:11:19.149
endowed with an insatiable appetite for human blood.

00:11:23.132 --> 00:11:25.794
The mosquito's proboscis is something very mobile.

00:11:26.855 --> 00:11:32.480
The mosquito will find the microcapillary where the blood passes using this very small channel.

00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:33.340
very, very weak.

00:11:35.581 --> 00:11:37.421
Females need blood,

00:11:37.701 --> 00:11:39.782
especially for the development of their eggs.

00:11:40.362 --> 00:11:43.623
So it is out of maternal instinct that the females bite.

00:11:43.802 --> 00:11:44.864
more than for sustenance.

00:11:47.864 --> 00:11:49.024
When the female bites,

00:11:49.785 --> 00:11:54.286
She injects saliva which thins the blood and allows it to be aspirated more easily.

00:11:56.647 --> 00:11:58.528
If the person is already infected with Zika,

00:11:59.388 --> 00:11:59.888
the insect...

00:12:00.087 --> 00:12:02.610
it sucks in the virus, which then multiplies in its stomach.

00:12:05.451 --> 00:12:05.952
Later,

00:12:06.212 --> 00:12:07.012
by pricking again,

00:12:07.634 --> 00:12:09.895
She injects the virus through her saliva.

00:12:10.435 --> 00:12:11.756
infecting its latest victim.

00:12:18.641 --> 00:12:20.843
Frédéric Simard is fascinated by these mosquitoes.

00:12:21.924 --> 00:12:25.226
His job, however, is to find new ways to exterminate them.

00:12:28.572 --> 00:12:33.416
We are going to expose mosquitoes to this insecticide.

00:12:33.417 --> 00:12:37.078
The insecticide we use on these mosquito nets is a neurotoxin.

00:12:37.399 --> 00:12:39.562
It will attach itself to the mosquito's neurons.

00:12:40.022 --> 00:12:43.024
The mosquito will be paralyzed and then die very quickly.

00:12:46.607 --> 00:12:49.149
His laboratory is developing new insecticides.

00:12:50.791 --> 00:12:53.714
When the first insecticides appeared in the 1940s,

00:12:54.453 --> 00:12:55.735
The mosquitoes seem to have been defeated.

00:12:56.896 --> 00:12:59.278
The rest of the story will not be so simple.

00:13:05.688 --> 00:13:06.790
In 1948,

00:13:07.450 --> 00:13:09.533
The WHO declares war on mosquitoes.

00:13:13.625 --> 00:13:15.305
The first effective insecticide,

00:13:15.565 --> 00:13:16.246
DDT,

00:13:17.006 --> 00:13:18.087
is at the heart of this struggle.

00:13:19.829 --> 00:13:20.870
We're spraying it everywhere,

00:13:21.350 --> 00:13:23.913
hunting down every last mosquito.

00:13:24.012 --> 00:13:24.612
To succeed,

00:13:25.093 --> 00:13:27.875
every drop of water must be drained or disinfected.

00:13:30.136 --> 00:13:31.257
Over vast areas,

00:13:31.437 --> 00:13:32.399
including Brazil,

00:13:32.818 --> 00:13:33.939
The mosquito has been eradicated.

00:13:36.121 --> 00:13:38.384
But the story takes a disastrous turn.

00:13:40.264 --> 00:13:43.125
DDT has proven to be toxic to human health.

00:13:43.887 --> 00:13:46.969
It was then gradually banned starting in the 1970s.

00:13:51.331 --> 00:13:51.853
But above all,

00:13:52.613 --> 00:13:54.334
The mosquito has found a way around it.

00:14:05.676 --> 00:14:07.878
And the phenomenon will relentlessly repeat itself.

00:14:08.738 --> 00:14:10.580
With each new insecticide produced,

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:14.462
Mosquitoes always manage to develop resistance.

00:14:23.995 --> 00:14:25.616
A female mosquito will lay eggs

00:14:25.996 --> 00:14:28.038
200 to 300 eggs every two days,

00:14:28.477 --> 00:14:34.520
This means that this resistance mechanism can very quickly invade an entire mosquito population.

00:14:38.962 --> 00:14:39.502
In one month,

00:14:40.023 --> 00:14:43.365
A resistant female can produce more than a million offspring.

00:14:49.307 --> 00:14:50.408
In 1980,

00:14:51.296 --> 00:14:53.422
The Aedes aegypti mosquito is back.

00:14:54.064 --> 00:14:57.032
ever more thirsty for conquests and new territories.

00:15:11.975 --> 00:15:16.038
Professor Dwayne Goebbler has been tracking mosquitoes around the world for 40 years.

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:20.741
If Aedes aegypti, the mosquito, had the ability to think,

00:15:21.121 --> 00:15:22.923
If he could think and reason like us,

00:15:23.403 --> 00:15:25.945
I certainly hope he would consider me his number one enemy.

00:15:26.345 --> 00:15:27.265
Let's get rid of this guy.

00:15:32.849 --> 00:15:33.149
Yet,

00:15:33.151 --> 00:15:33.750
retired,

00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:35.890
He returned to service upon the announcement of the epidemic.

00:15:38.448 --> 00:15:41.029
I would never have imagined it in 1971,

00:15:41.690 --> 00:15:45.092
when I started working on mosquito-borne diseases,

00:15:46.033 --> 00:15:47.214
that we would be faced,

00:15:47.414 --> 00:15:48.375
40 years later,

00:15:48.594 --> 00:15:49.975
to an even more serious problem.

00:15:53.078 --> 00:15:54.560
Every time I retire,

00:15:55.120 --> 00:15:56.341
A new epidemic is coming.

00:15:57.043 --> 00:15:59.225
I have to get back in the saddle and return to the fight.

00:16:04.310 --> 00:16:07.712
Dwayne Goebbler is monitoring the mosquito's spread in Florida.

00:16:11.084 --> 00:16:12.305
More than any other mosquito,

00:16:12.865 --> 00:16:15.086
The Aedes mosquito is adapted to living close to humans.

00:16:18.369 --> 00:16:21.791
And this behavior makes him a perfect carrier of disease.

00:16:25.913 --> 00:16:28.175
Aedes aegypti is a very silent mosquito.

00:16:29.536 --> 00:16:31.576
We don't hear it, and generally,

00:16:31.956 --> 00:16:32.998
You don't feel its sting.

00:16:34.199 --> 00:16:38.500
So if you are in a room with 5 or 6 people and only one Aedes aegypti mosquito,

00:16:39.862 --> 00:16:41.423
There's a good chance you'll all get stung.

00:16:42.184 --> 00:16:43.985
And if carriers of a virus like Zika,

00:16:44.546 --> 00:16:45.527
You will all be infected.

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:53.773
The spread of the Hedes mosquito throughout the world has always been a mystery.

00:16:54.373 --> 00:16:56.915
until Dwayne Goebbler helped solve it.

00:16:59.140 --> 00:16:59.260
There,

00:16:59.360 --> 00:17:03.121
You have the typical breeding site for Aedes aegypti.

00:17:03.921 --> 00:17:04.741
He loves tires.

00:17:05.342 --> 00:17:07.182
It's an ideal environment for larvae.

00:17:10.283 --> 00:17:12.504
Her eggs will hatch and in a few days,

00:17:12.844 --> 00:17:14.163
Adults will emerge.

00:17:14.663 --> 00:17:16.125
And that's where the problems begin.

00:17:20.046 --> 00:17:21.706
Aedes has a weakness for rubber.

00:17:23.647 --> 00:17:27.067
It likes to lay its eggs on the inner wall of used tires.

00:17:30.696 --> 00:17:32.478
The used tire market is booming.

00:17:33.979 --> 00:17:34.419
Each day,

00:17:34.619 --> 00:17:37.862
They are loaded by the millions onto cargo ships.

00:17:46.148 --> 00:17:47.711
And they crisscross the entire planet.

00:17:50.652 --> 00:17:52.894
And the mosquito travels with them.

00:17:56.553 --> 00:17:58.334
The tires are shipped worldwide.

00:17:58.953 --> 00:18:00.355
They carry the eggs with them.

00:18:00.914 --> 00:18:04.916
The eggs hatch and Aedes aegypti mosquitoes are introduced into a new region.

00:18:09.859 --> 00:18:14.222
The incredible network of global trade is one of the pillars of our modern society.

00:18:16.443 --> 00:18:19.645
But the mosquito has transformed it into a deadly ecosystem.

00:18:28.392 --> 00:18:29.693
They have existed for a long time.

00:18:29.973 --> 00:18:31.316
much longer than humans.

00:18:31.895 --> 00:18:34.658
It is likely that they will still be there when we are gone.

00:18:38.204 --> 00:18:41.246
The mosquito has thwarted all of man's attempts to annihilate it.

00:18:42.287 --> 00:18:43.928
But grappling with the Zika epidemic,

00:18:44.608 --> 00:18:47.150
The Brazilian government had no other choice but to try,

00:18:47.290 --> 00:18:47.971
Once again,

00:18:48.271 --> 00:18:48.951
to eradicate it.

00:18:50.813 --> 00:18:53.695
We are losing the battle against the mosquito.

00:18:54.455 --> 00:18:57.437
President Dilma Rousseff declares war on the mosquito.

00:18:58.078 --> 00:19:00.960
More than 200,000 soldiers have begun special training.

00:19:04.522 --> 00:19:04.942
This time,

00:19:05.122 --> 00:19:06.804
The target is not the adult mosquito.

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:08.460
But his descendants.

00:19:12.722 --> 00:19:13.422
In the favelas,

00:19:13.983 --> 00:19:16.123
The drinking water is infested with mosquito larvae.

00:19:20.285 --> 00:19:23.286
A new insecticide is then poured into all the tanks.

00:19:29.109 --> 00:19:31.370
But no one is certain that it will be effective.

00:19:33.951 --> 00:19:35.991
Then the tension turns towards the root of the problem.

00:19:49.613 --> 00:19:50.213
The virus itself.

00:19:50.233 --> 00:19:55.016
I live near this lake and I like to come here when I need to rest or find inspiration.

00:19:56.997 --> 00:19:59.057
When I first heard about Zika,

00:19:59.298 --> 00:20:02.759
I came here to reflect and I asked myself how I could help them.

00:20:07.300 --> 00:20:11.381
Ang Lee Tang immigrated from China to the United States to study viruses.

00:20:13.082 --> 00:20:14.442
Virology has always interested me.

00:20:14.922 --> 00:20:16.102
Viruses are so intelligent,

00:20:16.283 --> 00:20:17.223
if effective,

00:20:17.423 --> 00:20:17.943
It's fascinating.

00:20:24.805 --> 00:20:26.125
When Zika struck Brazil,

00:20:26.845 --> 00:20:29.666
His team is working on other mosquito-borne viruses.

00:20:33.287 --> 00:20:35.108
He stopped everything to dedicate himself to Zika.

00:20:38.204 --> 00:20:42.908
We had the opportunity to stop all our ongoing projects to dedicate ourselves immediately to Zika.

00:20:44.450 --> 00:20:44.570
Yes,

00:20:44.650 --> 00:20:45.370
I told my team,

00:20:46.131 --> 00:20:46.431
Let's go,

00:20:46.791 --> 00:20:48.092
Let's try to understand what's going on.

00:20:53.897 --> 00:20:56.379
The team wants to one day unravel the mystery of Zika.

00:20:58.241 --> 00:20:58.821
But very quickly,

00:20:58.822 --> 00:21:00.182
She encounters her first obstacle.

00:21:02.884 --> 00:21:05.747
Find enough samples of the virus to study it.

00:21:09.276 --> 00:21:11.217
It takes them weeks to obtain them.

00:21:12.097 --> 00:21:12.737
Because at the time,

00:21:12.998 --> 00:21:14.798
Very few laboratories are working on Zika.

00:21:18.440 --> 00:21:21.201
Working with the Zika virus potentially carries risks.

00:21:21.681 --> 00:21:22.661
And that worried us.

00:21:23.222 --> 00:21:25.963
Because a virus that can cause so much damage to a fetus's brain,

00:21:26.423 --> 00:21:27.243
We had never seen anything like it.

00:21:30.785 --> 00:21:31.845
What else can it cause?

00:21:32.505 --> 00:21:33.966
We wondered what could happen?

00:21:34.226 --> 00:21:35.146
What will we discover?

00:21:40.820 --> 00:21:41.681
To study Zika,

00:21:42.241 --> 00:21:44.222
They need a very large stock of viruses.

00:21:49.046 --> 00:21:53.369
They had already developed a rapid way to cultivate other mosquito-borne viruses.

00:21:54.530 --> 00:21:57.472
But they have no idea how effective it is against Zika.

00:22:03.957 --> 00:22:07.279
The method involves collecting cells from the stomach of a mosquito.

00:22:09.468 --> 00:22:13.292
then bathe them in a nutrient liquid where they can multiply.

00:22:16.856 --> 00:22:20.099
Then the Zika virus is added, in the hope that it will do its work.

00:22:21.120 --> 00:22:25.185
infect existing cells and thus multiply, like in a mosquito.

00:22:28.788 --> 00:22:30.750
But will this method work with Zika?

00:22:36.524 --> 00:22:37.385
For an entire weekend,

00:22:37.505 --> 00:22:39.085
by connecting every 6 hours,

00:22:39.665 --> 00:22:42.446
It was necessary to monitor these plaques of cells that contained the Zika virus.

00:22:43.866 --> 00:22:44.247
And finally,

00:22:44.248 --> 00:22:45.567
We thought we saw something.

00:22:45.907 --> 00:22:46.927
So we took the cells,

00:22:46.987 --> 00:22:48.288
They were placed under a microscope.

00:22:48.548 --> 00:22:50.508
We looked for the virus and we found it.

00:22:57.290 --> 00:23:02.652
Henry Tang and his team now have millions of Zika viruses at their disposal to experiment on.

00:23:06.405 --> 00:23:10.547
The most urgent question is to discover what happened in the brains of infants.

00:23:10.967 --> 00:23:11.667
like little Davy.

00:23:14.068 --> 00:23:16.710
Is the virus responsible for microcephaly?

00:23:18.931 --> 00:23:19.611
To find out,

00:23:20.191 --> 00:23:22.612
Professor Tang needs the help of a neurologist.

00:23:25.614 --> 00:23:29.576
It became clear at that moment that I needed to obtain brain cells.

00:23:36.613 --> 00:23:40.300
Professor Tang needs very specific brain cells.

00:23:42.163 --> 00:23:45.469
Cells that are identical in every way to those in the brain of a fetus.

00:23:47.143 --> 00:23:47.964
In 2016,

00:23:48.084 --> 00:23:49.205
He doesn't know it yet.

00:23:49.665 --> 00:23:50.786
but someone already owns one.

00:23:53.268 --> 00:23:54.308
As a scientist,

00:23:54.388 --> 00:23:57.130
We are always curious and drawn to mystery.

00:23:57.951 --> 00:24:02.334
The first time I saw images of these children born with microcephaly on the news,

00:24:02.874 --> 00:24:03.495
I thought to myself,

00:24:03.935 --> 00:24:05.516
Maybe I can do something.

00:24:09.099 --> 00:24:12.521
Neurologist Go Lee-Ming works with her husband Hong Jung-Sung.

00:24:16.063 --> 00:24:17.804
When Zika started to make headlines,

00:24:18.404 --> 00:24:20.565
They have just made an extraordinary breakthrough.

00:24:23.526 --> 00:24:29.047
They succeeded in creating fetal brains in the laboratory using stem cells.

00:24:31.688 --> 00:24:33.848
What's extraordinary about a stem cell,

00:24:34.349 --> 00:24:36.389
The reason is that it can be transformed into a heart cell.

00:24:36.629 --> 00:24:37.510
in liver cells,

00:24:37.530 --> 00:24:40.550
in pancreatic cells and of course in brain cells.

00:24:47.531 --> 00:24:48.652
How did they manage it?

00:24:50.394 --> 00:24:52.416
They took ordinary human skin cells.

00:24:54.038 --> 00:24:54.458
Afterwards,

00:24:55.038 --> 00:24:58.342
They genetically reprogrammed them to become stem cells.

00:25:02.466 --> 00:25:10.514
They then cultured these cells in a fluid containing exactly the same nutrients that the mother would provide to her fetus for brain development.

00:25:14.151 --> 00:25:17.372
The stem cells then develop into thin layers of brain cells.

00:25:24.054 --> 00:25:25.354
But they are not satisfied.

00:25:27.295 --> 00:25:30.155
because a brain is not just a thin layer of nerve cells.

00:25:32.076 --> 00:25:35.697
They need to find a way to make this brain grow in three dimensions.

00:25:37.137 --> 00:25:38.858
Which seems completely impossible to them.

00:25:41.238 --> 00:25:41.978
But one day,

00:25:42.439 --> 00:25:43.119
They have an idea.

00:25:44.751 --> 00:25:51.257
They are grown in suspension to make them rotate on their own axis, thus increasing their capacity to absorb oxygen and nutrients.

00:25:52.998 --> 00:25:54.880
To grow cells in suspension,

00:25:55.540 --> 00:25:59.043
They invent a small machine that rotates the cells without interruption.

00:26:02.345 --> 00:26:04.087
Everyone was very enthusiastic.

00:26:10.503 --> 00:26:11.004
From now on,

00:26:11.204 --> 00:26:13.245
we could develop mini-brains.

00:26:15.887 --> 00:26:16.868
Based on their experience,

00:26:17.168 --> 00:26:21.071
Go Lim In and Hong Jun Song have prepared new batches of stem cells.

00:26:23.712 --> 00:26:24.313
And this time,

00:26:24.553 --> 00:26:25.674
They place them in their device.

00:26:33.119 --> 00:26:34.180
For many long weeks,

00:26:34.360 --> 00:26:34.940
the cells,

00:26:35.000 --> 00:26:36.041
practically invisible,

00:26:36.461 --> 00:26:38.103
they go and go.

00:26:42.355 --> 00:26:43.155
They are growing up,

00:26:43.895 --> 00:26:46.896
They finally appear and become tiny globes.

00:26:50.797 --> 00:26:52.118
And inside these globes,

00:26:52.958 --> 00:26:54.839
They discover something remarkable.

00:26:56.859 --> 00:26:58.940
Cells do not just multiply.

00:27:01.060 --> 00:27:06.982
They begin to form the complex connections that a fetal brain already possesses at the beginning of pregnancy.

00:27:10.063 --> 00:27:10.803
Under the microscope,

00:27:11.204 --> 00:27:12.424
Multiple layers can be seen.

00:27:13.905 --> 00:27:15.346
We can see the stem cell layer,

00:27:16.266 --> 00:27:17.487
the layers of the different neurons.

00:27:18.567 --> 00:27:19.948
They form complex structures,

00:27:20.989 --> 00:27:22.970
exactly like in a developing human brain.

00:27:24.791 --> 00:27:27.232
They function like real nerve cells.

00:27:27.752 --> 00:27:29.393
They can send electrical signals to each other,

00:27:29.493 --> 00:27:31.394
as they would normally do in the brain.

00:27:40.299 --> 00:27:45.884
Go Lim In and Hong Joong Song have therefore succeeded in creating a fetal brain in the laboratory.

00:27:47.325 --> 00:27:47.805
Not one.

00:27:48.746 --> 00:27:49.507
but hundreds.

00:27:51.769 --> 00:27:53.891
Enough to test for the Zika virus.

00:27:55.392 --> 00:27:55.912
But for that to happen,

00:27:56.893 --> 00:27:58.454
They are still missing a major element.

00:27:59.776 --> 00:28:02.398
We started looking for where to obtain the Zika virus.

00:28:02.838 --> 00:28:07.602
The only answer we got was that we had to wait several months before the virus became available.

00:28:09.447 --> 00:28:15.093
So many scientists are working on Zika that there is now a long waiting list for virus samples.

00:28:17.435 --> 00:28:21.178
The two researchers are still unaware that Englitang possesses millions of them.

00:28:24.742 --> 00:28:26.303
For the two teams to meet,

00:28:26.684 --> 00:28:27.645
A crisis will be necessary.

00:28:30.855 --> 00:28:31.996
In March 2016,

00:28:32.616 --> 00:28:37.699
A group of environmentalists claims that the authorities are lying to the public about the causes of microcephaly.

00:28:38.499 --> 00:28:40.480
Zika is not responsible for this.

00:28:40.500 --> 00:28:40.960
he assures.

00:28:43.302 --> 00:28:44.602
The virus is a smokescreen.

00:28:45.383 --> 00:28:46.403
That's what they want us to believe.

00:28:47.784 --> 00:28:49.565
And it has become the biggest fraud in the world.

00:28:49.566 --> 00:28:53.707
Zika is not the cause of microcephaly.

00:28:55.888 --> 00:29:00.451
They blame the insecticide dumped in large quantities into drinking water in Brazil.

00:29:03.567 --> 00:29:05.127
Experts reject this argument.

00:29:06.468 --> 00:29:07.468
When you are a scientist,

00:29:07.908 --> 00:29:10.889
We shouldn't presume to think we have the right answer from the start.

00:29:11.349 --> 00:29:14.670
But we must also be careful not to get distracted by fanciful theories.

00:29:16.911 --> 00:29:18.511
That's always how it is in these kinds of cases.

00:29:19.351 --> 00:29:21.532
Alternative theories are emerging from all sides.

00:29:23.433 --> 00:29:27.194
It had become urgent to know whether the Zika virus caused microcephaly or not.

00:29:27.934 --> 00:29:31.775
Because the answer to this question would have a direct impact on public health policies.

00:29:35.335 --> 00:29:36.776
As tempers flare,

00:29:37.276 --> 00:29:42.340
Ang Lee Tang is desperately trying to find neurologists capable of testing his virus.

00:29:45.982 --> 00:29:46.363
A day,

00:29:46.523 --> 00:29:51.226
Hong Jun received an email from Ang Lee asking him who was the greatest expert on brain development.

00:29:52.447 --> 00:29:56.309
I called him immediately and my first question was, "Do you have the virus on hand?"

00:29:56.870 --> 00:29:58.051
And immediately on the phone,

00:29:58.191 --> 00:30:00.012
We made the decision to work together.

00:30:03.094 --> 00:30:04.135
In just a few days...

00:30:04.583 --> 00:30:06.445
The two teams begin their collaboration.

00:30:07.846 --> 00:30:09.747
We opened the box and took out the bottles.

00:30:10.368 --> 00:30:10.969
Inside,

00:30:10.989 --> 00:30:16.773
There were these little clusters of brain cells that were so developed that you could really see the little brains in the tubes.

00:30:21.498 --> 00:30:24.180
The experimental protocol is carefully designed.

00:30:25.301 --> 00:30:26.762
The result will be decisive.

00:30:29.725 --> 00:30:32.547
The virus is then added to half of the small brains.

00:30:34.967 --> 00:30:38.288
The other half serves as a control and develops normally.

00:30:40.409 --> 00:30:42.730
Will the presence of the virus make a difference?

00:30:45.171 --> 00:30:51.714
It's a rather nerve-wracking time because we had to incubate them with the Zika virus and wait for it to develop, and that...

00:30:52.574 --> 00:30:53.514
It takes a little time.

00:31:03.907 --> 00:31:07.029
Until we saw the effect the Zika virus had on them,

00:31:07.610 --> 00:31:08.590
And it was impressive.

00:31:10.632 --> 00:31:12.053
The result is indisputable.

00:31:12.673 --> 00:31:13.814
and even visible to the naked eye.

00:31:17.816 --> 00:31:19.337
The result exceeded all our expectations.

00:31:19.918 --> 00:31:22.239
Those who had been exposed to the virus were much smaller.

00:31:23.940 --> 00:31:24.641
One week later,

00:31:25.021 --> 00:31:27.603
They sent us a photo taken with a mobile phone.

00:31:28.771 --> 00:31:29.031
And then,

00:31:29.612 --> 00:31:31.553
The result was truly unequivocal.

00:31:32.914 --> 00:31:35.075
The Zika virus has been well linked to microcephaly.

00:31:35.115 --> 00:31:38.538
because his little brains were much smaller compared to normal brains.

00:31:43.241 --> 00:31:46.003
And the infected cells are not just smaller.

00:31:46.883 --> 00:31:47.604
Inside,

00:31:48.184 --> 00:31:50.626
Scientists are observing the damage caused by Zika.

00:31:57.851 --> 00:31:59.973
Once the virus reaches the fetus's brain,

00:32:00.954 --> 00:32:03.596
It is capable of attaching itself to developing nerve cells.

00:32:05.658 --> 00:32:10.523
The proteins present on the surface of the virus allow it to penetrate to the heart of the cell.

00:32:12.785 --> 00:32:12.905
There,

00:32:13.626 --> 00:32:15.667
He transforms it into a virus factory.

00:32:17.129 --> 00:32:19.111
The cell explodes and dies.

00:32:19.651 --> 00:32:21.753
The brain then stops developing.

00:32:21.973 --> 00:32:23.835
which leads to microcephaly.

00:32:24.763 --> 00:32:27.845
We immediately saw that the layers of neurons were much thinner.

00:32:28.266 --> 00:32:31.348
exactly like in babies with microcephaly.

00:32:32.349 --> 00:32:35.931
When we saw the images showing how badly the cells could be destroyed,

00:32:36.131 --> 00:32:40.835
It was chilling.

00:32:40.895 --> 00:32:41.555
Because suddenly,

00:32:42.216 --> 00:32:45.318
We have truly grasped the destructive power of this virus.

00:32:50.822 --> 00:32:52.363
Work on stem cells

00:32:52.807 --> 00:32:54.969
This is a huge turning point in Zika research.

00:32:57.191 --> 00:32:57.731
Now,

00:32:58.412 --> 00:33:02.055
Scientists are certain that Zika causes microcephaly.

00:33:03.196 --> 00:33:05.779
But as the contagion spreads far beyond Brazil,

00:33:06.239 --> 00:33:07.100
The news breaks.

00:33:08.001 --> 00:33:10.563
Zika virus transmission through sexual contact

00:33:10.603 --> 00:33:11.644
a proven case.

00:33:12.364 --> 00:33:16.468
A woman living in the capital is believed to have contracted Zika following sexual intercourse.

00:33:17.909 --> 00:33:19.451
If a man is infected with Zika...

00:33:20.403 --> 00:33:22.969
As we now know that it can be sexually transmitted,

00:33:23.812 --> 00:33:28.062
His partner may very well have never been in contact with a mosquito and still be infected.

00:33:28.884 --> 00:33:30.107
And this adds a significant risk of...

00:33:30.187 --> 00:33:31.928
additional to the Zika equation.

00:33:37.532 --> 00:33:38.212
Until Zika,

00:33:38.973 --> 00:33:43.175
No mosquito-borne virus was capable of being transmitted sexually.

00:33:44.516 --> 00:33:45.177
Then begins,

00:33:45.277 --> 00:33:46.097
around the world,

00:33:46.678 --> 00:33:50.440
a real race against time to find a solution to the Zika problem.

00:33:51.421 --> 00:33:51.921
A vaccine.

00:33:53.262 --> 00:33:55.143
More than 20 different groups get to work.

00:33:56.839 --> 00:34:00.420
At the heart of their entire project lies a surprisingly simple principle.

00:34:02.261 --> 00:34:04.862
A principle invented at the Pasteur Institute,

00:34:05.282 --> 00:34:08.684
where the method for creating a vaccine originated more than a century ago.

00:34:10.244 --> 00:34:11.005
The idea of ​​the vaccine,

00:34:11.645 --> 00:34:19.068
It's about presenting the immune system with components of the virus that will cause the immune system to develop a response.

00:34:22.469 --> 00:34:26.191
Vaccines train our immune system to recognize a microbe.

00:34:26.623 --> 00:34:29.244
to trigger an immediate response and eliminate it.

00:34:32.425 --> 00:34:34.045
To manufacture an effective vaccine,

00:34:34.585 --> 00:34:40.027
We need to find the part of the virus that is capable of triggering a massive defense response from our body.

00:34:44.808 --> 00:34:45.729
Once identified,

00:34:46.629 --> 00:34:48.309
it is in a non-infectious form,

00:34:48.650 --> 00:34:50.930
that is to say, something that cannot reproduce in the body,

00:34:51.390 --> 00:34:53.231
that the virus element is injected.

00:34:58.583 --> 00:35:00.103
During the actual encounter with the virus,

00:35:00.924 --> 00:35:02.804
The body is then ready to reject it.

00:35:03.444 --> 00:35:04.064
He is vaccinated.

00:35:05.425 --> 00:35:06.205
In 2016,

00:35:06.805 --> 00:35:09.686
Progress on the Zika vaccine is rapid.

00:35:11.366 --> 00:35:15.988
There are already trials today, called phase 1 trials, to see if the vaccine is well tolerated.

00:35:16.568 --> 00:35:21.109
There is even a phase 2 trial where they are seeing if it induces an immune response that could be protective.

00:35:21.369 --> 00:35:22.449
And that's in humans.

00:35:24.010 --> 00:35:25.190
But despite these advances,

00:35:25.770 --> 00:35:28.051
Developing a vaccine against Zika presents enormous challenges.

00:35:29.295 --> 00:35:29.795
Among other things,

00:35:30.156 --> 00:35:33.138
Clinical trials must be conducted on thousands of people.

00:35:34.739 --> 00:35:37.461
And they must include women of childbearing age.

00:35:40.263 --> 00:35:42.725
We have clearly seen that the main complication of the Zika virus,

00:35:43.245 --> 00:35:46.968
These are neurological disorders in children born to mothers infected during pregnancy.

00:35:47.648 --> 00:35:48.529
So it is the women,

00:35:48.609 --> 00:35:50.510
even before they are old enough to reproduce,

00:35:50.811 --> 00:35:52.452
who will be the target of this vaccine.

00:35:55.214 --> 00:35:56.875
Testing a vaccine on young girls...

00:35:57.423 --> 00:35:59.444
means years of waiting for the results.

00:36:02.425 --> 00:36:06.766
And the decision to produce a vaccine on a mass scale also depends on the extent of the epidemic.

00:36:11.287 --> 00:36:12.808
In the middle of 2017,

00:36:13.408 --> 00:36:17.149
Zika managed to cross the Atlantic to reach the African coast.

00:36:17.749 --> 00:36:19.550
one of the most populated regions on the globe.

00:36:22.231 --> 00:36:23.591
He returned to his roots.

00:36:27.003 --> 00:36:29.124
Will Zika cause an epidemic in Africa?

00:36:30.465 --> 00:36:33.827
This is a question that Sarah Salinas attempts to answer.

00:36:35.107 --> 00:36:35.488
For her,

00:36:35.768 --> 00:36:37.129
The answer lies hidden in the past.

00:36:38.009 --> 00:36:40.770
at a time when Zika was already present on the continent,

00:36:41.151 --> 00:36:42.191
several decades ago.

00:36:44.553 --> 00:36:47.774
But why has no trace of microcephaly ever been found there?

00:36:49.715 --> 00:36:56.279
One of the questions scientists have asked is whether the Zika strain has evolved.

00:36:56.559 --> 00:36:59.642
compared to the strain originally discovered in Africa,

00:36:59.942 --> 00:37:01.303
and had become more toxic.

00:37:02.624 --> 00:37:05.146
Sarah Salinas knows that the Zika virus,

00:37:05.246 --> 00:37:06.767
which caused the epidemic in Brazil,

00:37:07.288 --> 00:37:10.290
is slightly different from the virus found in Africa.

00:37:13.073 --> 00:37:16.616
Could this difference explain the danger of the Brazilian virus?

00:37:20.439 --> 00:37:25.223
The initial idea was to try to compare this toxicity.

00:37:25.703 --> 00:37:31.347
between the African strain and the strain that was also responsible for the epidemic in Brazil.

00:37:33.748 --> 00:37:34.829
Early 2017,

00:37:35.189 --> 00:37:37.851
The Salinas team already has the Brazilian virus.

00:37:40.172 --> 00:37:42.173
But to reconstruct the evolution of Zika,

00:37:42.894 --> 00:37:46.316
They need the African virus that was circulating several decades ago.

00:37:47.897 --> 00:37:48.577
And the problem,

00:37:49.017 --> 00:37:49.698
that's because at the time,

00:37:50.178 --> 00:37:51.299
No one was studying Zika.

00:37:54.419 --> 00:37:57.600
The search for the African strain continued for months.

00:38:00.421 --> 00:38:00.782
Finally,

00:38:01.202 --> 00:38:01.922
He's nearing his goal.

