00:39:54.750 --> 00:39:57.771
So why has there been no microcephaly in Africa?

00:40:01.479 --> 00:40:06.461
One possible reason could be the development of natural immunity in the African population.

00:40:07.101 --> 00:40:08.702
following a very old epidemic.

00:40:10.843 --> 00:40:14.304
And the number of microcephaly cases would therefore have fallen rapidly.

00:40:15.845 --> 00:40:17.846
What is troubling about microcephaly,

00:40:18.646 --> 00:40:20.847
The reason is that it can be caused by many factors.

00:40:22.208 --> 00:40:25.349
And the reason why we didn't make the connection with Zika earlier,

00:40:26.890 --> 00:40:29.331
This is because Zika existed in an endemic form.

00:40:30.211 --> 00:40:31.552
and not in an eruptive form,

00:40:32.213 --> 00:40:33.554
That is to say, there was no epidemic.

00:40:34.815 --> 00:40:38.058
It is therefore possible that there have been cases of microcephaly linked to Zika.

00:40:38.719 --> 00:40:42.683
but they could not be distinguished from microcephaly caused by other causes.

00:40:51.451 --> 00:40:53.493
If the Brazilian strain spreads to Africa,

00:40:54.213 --> 00:40:55.795
Nobody knows what might happen.

